================================================================================
Title: Stellar Yields of Rotating First Stars. II. Pair Instability Supernovae 
       and Comparison with Observations 
Authors: Takahashi K., Yoshida T., Umeda H. 
================================================================================
Description of contents: Yields of 18 Pop III PISN models are provided.
    Initial mass range from 180 to 280 Msun for non-rotating models, from
    160to 260 Msun for magnetic rotating models, and from 160 to 260 Msun
    for non-magnetic rotating models.

    The files include are:

    mr160.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=160 Msun
    mr180.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=180 Msun
    mr200.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=200 Msun
    mr220.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=220 Msun
    mr240.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=240 Msun
    mr260.txt = PISN Yields of the magnetic rotating model; Mini=260 Msun
    nm160.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=160 Msun
    nm180.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=180 Msun
    nm200.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=200 Msun
    nm220.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=220 Msun
    nm240.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=240 Msun
    nm260.txt = PISN Yields of the non-magnetic rotating model; Mini=260 Msun
    nr180.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=180 Msun
    nr200.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=200 Msun
    nr220.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=220 Msun
    nr240.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=240 Msun
    nr260.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=260 Msun
    nr280.txt = PISN Yields of the non-rotating model; Mini=280 Msun
    
System requirements: The files are formatted according to the machine
    readable format used by the AAS Journals and CDS/VizieR. Specific
    information on the structure of MRT files can be found at:

        AAS: http://journals.aas.org/authors/MRT/
        CDS: http://cds.u-strasbg.fr/doc/catstd.htx

    These files can be read in python using the astropy package:

        from astropy.table import Table
        data = Table.read("nr280.txt", format="ascii.cds")

Additional comments: (No comments)
================================================================================
